  "changes": [
    "Relocate original arm64e DWARF CIE personality and FDE LSDA PC-relative fields while code, LSDA storage and authenticated personality slots retain their addresses.",
    "Retain fixed-width signed 32/64-bit or Darwin PC-relative absptr encoding, null augmentation pointers, normalized CFI and every statically known return-address signing state; refuse moved-EH targets, unsupported encodings, dynamic CFI and out-of-range displacements.",
    "Use 65-bit pointer-difference arithmetic to avoid signed overflow at the uint64 address boundary.",
    "Recognize ld-classic ARM64 DWARF side-table LSDAs without UNWIND_HAS_LSDA through one architecture-aware loader rule shared by rewriting and replay; preserve the original encoding and keep generated-record contracts strict.",
    "Force original compiler catch/cleanup frames to move in O0/O2 chained/threaded native installation fixtures, preserving language identity and independently validating the output.",
    "Require nontrivial signatures and successful valid authentication for IA/IB/DA/DB plus a fault from corrupted signatures. A flushed main-entry marker distinguishes unavailable startup from a failed running probe. Unexpected key failures take precedence over unavailable keys.",
    "Check original caught and propagated cleanup paths alongside installed native functions after the capability gate; keep file checks distinct from runtime qualification."
  ],
